        },
        "heading_iJ7P7D": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "<em><strong>Here's everything I tried (and why none of it worked):</strong></em>",
            "heading_size": "title-sm",
            "heading_tag": "h2",
            "highlighted_text": "marker",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle",
            "highlighted_reveal": false
          }
        },
        "text_g7DibU": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>The posture brace ($25–$45)</p>",
            "text_font": "body",
            "text_size": "subtext-sm",
            "text_max_size": 32,
            "text_line_height": 1.6,
            "text_letter_spacing": 0,
            "text_capitalize": false,
            "secondary_color": false,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "text_ywhYhi": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>I wore mine religiously for 6 weeks. It felt like it was helping — until I took it off and the hump was exactly the same. Worse, actually. A brace holds your shoulders back, but it doesn't touch the muscle that's pulling your head forward. It's like putting a cast on a muscle that needs to be released. And while you wear it, your own muscles get weaker because the brace is doing their job.</p>",
            "text_font": "body",
            "text_size": "subtext-md",
            "text_max_size": 32,
            "text_line_height": 1.6,
            "text_letter_spacing": 0,
            "text_capitalize": false,
            "secondary_color": false,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        }
      },
