    "image_with_text_Hzd6kr": {
      "type": "image-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "text_JXFiiL": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Chin tucks and YouTube stretches (free)</p>",
            "text_font": "body",
            "text_size": "subtext-sm",
            "text_max_size": 32,
            "text_line_height": 1.6,
            "text_letter_spacing": 0,
            "text_capitalize": false,
            "secondary_color": true,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "text_RqY6DM": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>I saved the video. I did the routine for about 9 days. Sound familiar? Even if you stuck with it, chin tucks stretch the back of the neck — but they don't release the muscle on the <em>front</em> of the neck that's actually pulling everything forward. You're stretching a rope that's already knotted.</p>",
            "text_font": "body",
            "text_size": "subtext-md",
            "text_max_size": 32,
            "text_line_height": 1.6,
            "text_letter_spacing": 0,
            "text_capitalize": false,
            "secondary_color": false,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "text_3Ntj3D": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>The chiropractor ($75/visit, $1,200+/year)</p>",
            "text_font": "body",
            "text_size": "subtext-sm",
            "text_max_size": 32,
            "text_line_height": 1.6,
            "text_letter_spacing": 0,
            "text_capitalize": false,
            "secondary_color": false,
            "highlighted_text": "marker",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "text_V3jeCg": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>I went 8 times. Each visit felt amazing for about 48 hours. Then the hump was back. The adjustment moves the bones — but nobody was releasing the muscle that was pulling those bones back out of alignment. So the adjustment reverses itself. Every single time. An endless cycle at $75 a pop.<br/></p>",
            "text_font": "body",
            "text_size": "subtext-md",
            "text_max_size": 32,
            "text_line_height": 1.6,
            "text_letter_spacing": 0,
            "text_capitalize": false,
            "secondary_color": false,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "text_DrMh3V": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Cervical pillows ($30–$60)</p>",
            "text_font": "body",
            "text_size": "subtext-sm",
            "text_max_size": 32,
            "text_line_height": 1.6,
            "text_letter_spacing": 0,
            "text_capitalize": false,
            "secondary_color": false,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "text_9JACVt": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>A better pillow supports your neck while you sleep. That's real. But it doesn't release the locked-up muscle during the day. It's treating a symptom of a symptom of the actual cause. Three layers removed from the problem.</p>",
            "text_font": "body",
            "text_size": "subtext-md",
            "text_max_size": 32,
            "text_line_height": 1.6,
            "text_letter_spacing": 0,
            "text_capitalize": false,
            "secondary_color": false,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "text_jGKXzX": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Neck hump creams and patches ($15–$50)</p>",
            "text_font": "body",
            "text_size": "subtext-sm",
            "text_max_size": 32,
            "text_line_height": 1.6,
            "text_letter_spacing": 0,
            "text_capitalize": false,
            "secondary_color": false,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "text_bbTH3t": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>I'm not going to mock this because I bought one too. We all want it to be that simple. But a cream on your skin cannot physically release a deep muscle under your spine. It just can't.</p>",
            "text_font": "body",
            "text_size": "subtext-md",
            "text_max_size": 32,
            "text_line_height": 1.6,
            "text_letter_spacing": 0,
            "text_capitalize": false,
            "secondary_color": false,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "button_n6PLVw": {
          "type": "button",
          "settings": {
            "button_label": "So What Actually Works?",
            "button_link": "shopify://products/neck-massager",
            "button_style": "primary",
            "button_size": "md",
            "button_external": false,
            "button_icon": true
          }
        },
        "heading_UWHXaT": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "<em><strong>Then a physical therapist told me something nobody else had.</strong></em>",
            "heading_size": "title-md",
            "heading_tag": "h2",
            "highlighted_text": "marker",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle",
            "highlighted_reveal": false
          }
        },
        "text_yYgWrq": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>She said: \"The problem isn't your posture. It's a muscle.\"</p><p>There's a muscle on the front of your neck called the <strong>SCM — the sternocleidomastoid</strong>. You've never heard of it. Neither had I.</p><p>Every hour you spend looking at a screen — your phone, your laptop, your monitor — this muscle tightens. It shortens. And it physically <strong>pulls your head forward and down</strong>, forcing your upper spine to curve into that visible hump.</p>",
            "text_font": "body",
            "text_size": "subtext-sm",
            "text_max_size": 32,
            "text_line_height": 1.6,
            "text_letter_spacing": 0,
            "text_capitalize": false,
            "secondary_color": false,
            "highlighted_text": "marker",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "image_YFAJHY": {
          "type": "image",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/8b363bb4a3a0200e60fcf88a6dfb8ff3.jpg",
            "image_width": "full_width",
            "image_max_width": 1000,
            "image_max_width_mobile": 100
          }
        },
        "text_DzjTBz": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>The sternocleidomastoid (SCM) — the muscle responsible for pulling your head forward<br/></p>",
            "text_font": "body",
            "text_size": "subtext-sm",
            "text_max_size": 32,
            "text_line_height": 1.6,
            "text_letter_spacing": 0,
            "text_capitalize": false,
            "secondary_color": false,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "text_Ar7Tby": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>That's why the brace didn't work — it held your shoulders but never touched the SCM.</p><p>That's why the chiropractor's adjustment reversed — the bones were moved, but the muscle pulling them forward was never released.</p><p>That's why stretches felt good for a day — you were loosening the <em>back</em> of the neck while the <em>front</em> stayed locked tight.</p><p><strong>Every solution you've tried has treated the result of this muscle locking up. None of them treated the muscle itself.</strong></p><p>Once I understood this, the question changed. It wasn't \"how do I fix my posture\" anymore. It was: <strong>\"how do I get this muscle to let go?\"</strong></p>",
            "text_font": "body",
            "text_size": "subtext-sm",
            "text_max_size": 32,
            "text_line_height": 1.6,
            "text_letter_spacing": 0,
            "text_capitalize": false,
            "secondary_color": false,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "button_HTEacw": {
          "type": "button",
          "settings": {
            "button_label": "See the Device That Targets the SCM",
            "button_link": "shopify://products/neck-massager",
            "button_style": "primary",
            "button_size": "md",
            "button_external": false,
            "button_icon": true
          }
        },
        "text_bjz9ne": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Clinical-grade SCM release · 180-day money-back guarantee</p>",
            "text_font": "heading",
            "text_size": "subtext-sm",
            "text_max_size": 32,
            "text_line_height": 1.6,
            "text_letter_spacing": 0,
            "text_capitalize": false,
            "secondary_color": true,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "heading_9YgCCq": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "<em><strong>There are really only 3 ways to release the SCM.</strong></em>",
            "heading_size": "title-md",
            "heading_tag": "h2",
            "highlighted_text": "marker",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle",
            "highlighted_reveal": false
          }
        },
        "text_XtFnRd": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<h3>Option 1: Manual therapy (PT or specialized massage)</h3><p>This works. A skilled therapist can physically grip the SCM and release it. The problem is cost and access. Sessions run $125–$290 each. A full treatment protocol is 9–12 months. Total cost: $1,500–$3,500. And you have to go to someone's office, on their schedule, in their city. It works. Most people simply can't sustain it.</p><h3>Option 2: Do nothing and hope it resolves</h3><p>The SCM doesn't relax on its own — not while you're still using screens 8+ hours a day. Every month you wait, the muscle locks tighter, the curve deepens, and the hump becomes more visible. What looks like a cosmetic issue at 38 can become a structural problem by 48. The trajectory only goes one direction.</p>",
            "text_font": "body",
            "text_size": "subtext-md",
            "text_max_size": 32,
            "text_line_height": 1.6,
            "text_letter_spacing": 0,
            "text_capitalize": false,
            "secondary_color": false,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "image_w4TApY": {
          "type": "image",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/fbfa96c7134874bbd72e4a3e01bde673.jpg",
            "image_width": "full_width",
            "image_max_width": 50,
            "image_max_width_mobile": 50
          }
        },
        "text_VWAzff": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<h3>Option 3: Replicate the SCM release at home</h3><p>This is what I found. A clinical-grade device that physically grips and decompresses the SCM — the same technique a therapist performs — but at home, in 10 minutes, lying in bed before sleep. Combined with 42°C therapeutic heat that softens the tissue so the release penetrates deeper.</p><p>One device. $200 once. No appointments. No recurring cost. No schedule.</p><p>It's called QuestProps.</p>",
            "text_font": "heading",
            "text_size": "subtext-md",
            "text_max_size": 32,
            "text_line_height": 1.6,
            "text_letter_spacing": 0,
            "text_capitalize": false,
            "secondary_color": false,
            "highlighted_text": "marker",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "button_dTXjMC": {
          "type": "button",
          "settings": {
            "button_label": "See If QuestProps Is Right For You",
            "button_link": "shopify://products/neck-massager",
            "button_style": "primary",
            "button_size": "sm",
            "button_external": false,
            "button_icon": true
          }
        },
        "text_p8jqAi": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>180-day money-back guarantee · Free shipping</p>",
            "text_font": "heading",
            "text_size": "subtext-sm",
            "text_max_size": 32,
            "text_line_height": 1.6,
            "text_letter_spacing": 0,
            "text_capitalize": false,
